  "name": "Vocal Growl Gnash",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A talking tearout growl. A drawn half-note pattern opens and closes a vowel-like mouth over FM grit, with a clean mono sub underneath. Play it low (F1 to A#1) as sparse stabs or held notes at 140 to 150 BPM and the pattern restarts on every note. Growl pushes how hard the pattern bites the tone and the FM, Vowel moves the mouth shape, Grit drives the distortion harder, and Width spreads the top above 120 Hz while the low end stays mono.",
  "category": "Bass/tearout",
